    "title": "Patriots’ Mike Vrabel, Dianna Russini respond to affair rumors",
    "text": "Mike Vrabel and Dianna Russini are reacting to viral photos of the pair at a resort. In photos obtained by Page Six, the outlet described the New England Patriots head coach as “holding hands and hugging” Dianna Russini at a luxury resort. The two were spotted two weekends ago at the Ambiente in Sedona, Arizona. While some fans interpreted the gestures as romantic between the two — both Vrabel and Russini are married to other people — they quickly responded to the noise and debunked those rumors.“The photos don’t represent the group of six people who were hanging out during the day. Like most journalists in the NFL, reporters interact with sources away from stadiums and other venues.” Russini reportedly said per The Daily Mail.Vrabel also responded to the images in agreement with Russini.“These photos show a completely innocent interaction and any suggestion otherwise is laughable. This doesn’t deserve any further response.” Vrabel reportedly said per The Daily Mail.Russini is currently employed at The Athletic, where she is a senior NFL insider, and they also shared a statement about the photos.“These photos are misleading and lack essential context,” Steven Ginsberg, executive editor of The Athletic, told the Post. “These were public interactions in front of many people. Dianna is a premier journalist covering the NFL and we’re proud to have her at The Athletic.”The photos are reportedly a misunderstanding as they both arrived separately with a separate group of friends. Vrabel has been married to Jen Vrabel since 1999. As for Russini, she married her husband, Kevin Goldschmidt, in 2020.Russini was previously an anchor on ESPN’s flagship SportsCenter before she was hired at The Athletic in 2023. As for Vrabel, who led the Patriots to their first Super Bowl since 2019, was hired as the Patriots' head coach in January 2025. The former NFL linebacker played for the Patriots for eight seasons from 2001 to 2008. Prior to playng for the Patriots, he was on the Pittsburgh Steelers roster from 1997 to 2000 and played for the Kansas City Chiefs from 2009-2010. During his time at the Patriots, he won three Super Bowls. Mike Vrabel and Dianna Russini are reacting to viral photos of the pair at a resort. In photos obtained by Page Six, the outlet described the New England Patriots head coach as &#8220;holding hands and hugging&#8221; Dianna Russini at a luxury resort. The two were spotted two weekends ago at the Ambiente in Sedona, Arizona.",
